There are now programs to automatically re-run NetHack until certain stats
are achieved (I do it by hand - that, I feel is fair).

I think a set number of "points" should be allowed, and the player may
assign them as she wishes.  Basically, just a generalization of the "wish"
concept.  It could even be used to DECREASE the power of the "wish" concept
(which I think is far too chaotic in nature):  only the WoW in the castle
[right?  I've never been there] should be a powerful WoW.  And allow wishing
for attributes - perhaps only at the start of the game.


... then again... that wish-parser is pretty wild code!!


